PKGBUILD_REQUEST(3)

# NAME

pkgbuild_request - seal complete native build inputs

# DESCRIPTION

*build_request::seal* accepts one *pkgsource::source_snapshot*, all materialized
source inputs, all materialized build and check package inputs, selected build
and target architectures, and one *build_policy*.

Every source declaration must have exactly one verified materialization. Every
expanded build and check package requirement must have exactly one input in the
matching scope. Extra, missing, duplicate, or cross-scope bindings are rejected.
Selected architectures must satisfy the source-owned architecture constraints.

The request retains source-owned package release, recipe and snapshot
identities, exact build-program bytes, selected build profiles and provenance,
source material, build/check inputs, architectures, and policy.

Requirement and source collections are normalized where order is not semantic.
Program bytes are preserved exactly.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgbuild*(3), *pkgbuild_model*(3), *pkgbuild_result*(3)
